'\"
.TH "rbc::GRID" 3tcl 0\&.5\&.0 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::GRID - Commands in namespace rbc::GRID
.SH "GRAPH GRID GRID COMMAND"
.PP
Commands in this namespace document the graph grid\&.
.PP
GRID is used below as a placeholder for:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
GRAPHINST grid
.fi
.RE
.PP
The grid draws horizontal and vertical lines across the plotting area at axis tick positions\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
graph \&.g
\&.g grid configure -hide no -color grey70 -dashes dot
.fi
.RE
.PP
The grid is a single component of the graph\&. Unlike elements, markers, or pens, there are no named grid
objects\&.
.SH "GRID AXES"
.PP
-mapx and -mapy select the axes whose tick positions are used to generate the grid\&.
.PP
-mapx controls the vertical grid lines:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid configure -mapx x
.fi
.RE
.PP
-mapy controls the horizontal grid lines:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid configure -mapy y
.fi
.RE
.PP
Either mapping may be empty to disable grid lines for that direction:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid configure -mapx {}
.fi
.RE
.PP
This is especially useful for bar charts, where the default grid uses only the Y axis\&.
.PP
The axis names refer to graph axes documented by \fIAXIS\fP\&.
.SH "MAJOR AND MINOR GRID LINES"
.PP
Grid lines normally follow both major and minor axis ticks\&.
.PP
The -minor option controls whether lines are also drawn at minor tick positions:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid configure -minor no
.fi
.RE
.PP
With -minor no, only major tick positions generate grid lines\&. With -minor yes, minor tick positions are
included as well\&.
.PP
The number and spacing of the grid lines therefore depend on the tick configuration of the mapped axes\&.
.SH "SHOWING AND HIDING THE GRID"
.PP
The -hide option controls grid visibility:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid configure -hide no
.fi
.RE
.PP
The GRID on, GRID off, and GRID toggle operations provide convenient alternatives:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid on
\&.g grid off
\&.g grid toggle
.fi
.RE
.PP
These operations change the same state represented by -hide\&. For example, after:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid off
.fi
.RE
.PP
querying:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g grid cget -hide
.fi
.RE
.PP
returns a true value\&.
.SH "WIDGET-SPECIFIC DEFAULTS"
.PP
The initial grid configuration depends on the graph widget type\&.
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l l l.
Widget| -hide | -mapx | -mapy
_
graph| yes| x| y
stripchart | yes| x| y
barchart| no| empty| y
.TE
.PP
Thus a graph or stripchart does not initially display its grid, while a barchart initially displays
horizontal grid lines associated with its Y axis\&.
.PP
The remaining grid defaults are common to all graph widget types\&.
.SH "GRID OPTIONS"
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-color color | Specifies the color of the grid lines\&. The default is grey64 on color displays and black on monochrome displays\&.
-dashes dashList| Specifies the dash pattern used for grid lines\&. The default is dot\&. An empty value selects solid lines\&.
-hide boolean| Specifies whether the grid is hidden\&. The default is yes for graph and stripchart, and no for barchart\&.
-linewidth distance | Specifies the width of the grid lines as a non-negative screen distance\&. Values 0 and 1 use the native thin-line representation\&. The default is 0\&.
-mapx axisName | Specifies the X axis whose tick positions generate vertical grid lines\&. The axis must exist and must be an X axis\&. An empty value disables vertical grid lines\&. The default is x for graph and stripchart, and empty for barchart\&.
-mapy axisName | Specifies the Y axis whose tick positions generate horizontal grid lines\&. The axis must exist and must be a Y axis\&. An empty value disables horizontal grid lines\&. The default is y\&.
-minor boolean| Specifies whether grid lines are also generated at minor tick positions\&. The default is yes\&.
.TE
.PP
Grid configuration options may also be supplied through Tk's option database\&. The resource name is grid and
the resource class is Grid\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
option add *Graph\&.grid\&.Color grey70
option add *Graph\&.Grid\&.Linewidth 1
.fi
.RE

